    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter August 17th with a primary offensive engine fueled by favorable matchups against elevated xERA starters. **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) headlines our lineup, benefiting from a potent combination of a 4.93 xERA opponent and a high-efficiency park factor that boosts his output by 14%. **Andy Pages** (74.43) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.20) round out our top-tier tier starts; both leverage the same 4.93 xERA target in **Andy Pages**\u2019 case, while **Drake Baldwin** maximizes his value through a prime leadoff spot against a 4.81 xERA pitcher, ensuring consistent volume in a high-upside matchup. \n\nWhile we are leaning into favorable park environments for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, we must navigate a few suboptimal platoon scenarios. **Gunnar Henderson** (52.61) remains a start, but his efficiency is suppressed by a 15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against McClanahan. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** (48.29) faces a tough L/L matchup against Shota Imanaga. The decision to start **Jacob Wilson** (59.20) over potential depth options was driven by his high base floor and strong SP skill adjustment, narrowly missing the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold but remaining the most reliable SS option. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, though players like **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** were reviewed as bench alternatives; none offered the necessary ceiling to displace the current starters today. Please note that all lineup slots are currently based on projected batting orders; any mid-day shifts to the bottom of the order for **Liam Hicks** or **Coby Mayo** could further compress their marginal scores and threaten their starting status before first pitch.",
